1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,374
Every family has a beginning. Ours
begins at the old walls of Harar.

2
00:00:07,074 --> 00:00:13,336
My great-grandparents came here as
strangers, carrying little more than a

3
00:00:13,336 --> 00:00:13,858
skill.

4
00:00:14,557 --> 00:00:19,689
They were tailors. Stitch by stitch,
they built a life with their hands.

5
00:00:20,557 --> 00:00:25,325
My grandmother kept a small stall by the
street. The stitches became trade, and

6
00:00:25,325 --> 00:00:26,914
the trade became a living.

7
00:00:27,614 --> 00:00:32,021
For the ones who would come after them,
they saved what they earned.

8
00:00:33,114 --> 00:00:39,126
My mother worked in the market by day,
and carried her schoolbooks with her.

9
00:00:39,826 --> 00:00:44,318
At night, when she was tired, she
studied anyway.

10
00:00:45,826 --> 00:00:48,685
And one day, she graduated.

11
00:00:51,826 --> 00:00:57,174
Then she worked long hours in an office,
and gave everything she had so that I

12
00:00:57,174 --> 00:00:58,008
could learn.

13
00:00:58,826 --> 00:01:05,069
I graduated in software engineering with
honours, won a scholarship for my

14
00:01:05,069 --> 00:01:10,969
master's, and today I am an AI engineer,
with comforts they never had.

15
00:01:11,669 --> 00:01:18,242
Nothing I have is mine alone. It is the
work of everyone who came before me. Now

16
00:01:18,242 --> 00:01:21,653
it is my turn to take us a little
further.

